# nir/lower_blend: Store according to present component offsets
# https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/39419 state=opened
# ### What does this MR do and why?
<!-- Describe in detail what your merge request does and why. -->

```
nir/lower_blend: Store according to present component offsets

store_output intrinsics may contain a non-zero component. Without this
change nir_lower_blend would always try to store the whole vector
disregarding the component present in the intrinsic. Led to situations
where the render target is RGBA, store_output contains component 1 with
write_mask x (so a single channel G). After the blend pass, the
store_output would be the same but the src being a vec4 which breaks
nir validation because instr->num_components (4) + component > 4.

Along with the mentioned issue, when loading the input for the previous
case it would be loaded as R due to how the padding for the input is done.
This change handles these cases too by applying the component to offset
the values when loading the input.

Signed-off-by: Aitor Camacho <aitor@lunarg.com>
```

KK recently started running debug builds in our internal CI and we are running into nir validation errors with `dEQP-VK.glsl.440.linkage.varying.component.frag_out.vec3.as_float_float_float`. This seems to only be a nir validation issue. Looking for feedback if this is a reasonable approach to fix the observed issues or if there is an already existing pass that handles this (or maybe we should not end up in a state that allows the mentioned behavior).

